 go straight up from the  base of a mountain when you're trapped  by the final circle the only other  really notable item in the game for  getting around is the bounce pad which  you may find randomly in the environment  the balance pad can be placed on a floor  and will eject players into the air  allowing them to open their glider and  go long distances it's the closest thing  you'll find to a vehicle from pub G  once you've mastered those basic shapes  you're ready for panic forts which is  what you build when somebody shoots at  you and you have no idea where they are  to make the basic fort put up one or two  ramps in a v-shape then add one two two  stories of walls on top of it while on  top of your ramp leap up and lay down  more ramps below you which makes your  fort stronger and prevents people from  coming up from under you you'll use the  same template for taller towers and it's  a great way to get building into your  muscle memory speaking of if you've  collected some good loot made it to the  final circle and now all the players  around you are suddenly going vertical  before heading up yourself understand  how to cut down enemy forts the new mini  gun makes this a lot easier as well as  explosives aimed at the base this is  because if you shoot out the bottom of  the fort you can actually drop the  entire thing also if the enemy team is  building up and out shoot out the floor  from beneath them to drop them out of  their own Tower and do some damage when  it comes time to building your own Tower  make sure the base is made of stone or  metal so it's less likely to be taken  out from under you use the same method  as your panic for it to build high then  at the top flip some ramps into an open  bowl your fort will end up looking a bit  like a flower this is a great bill for  playing with squads  with wide commanding views of an entire  area and that you get you started with  combat building in fortnight veteran  players what fortifications do you like 